  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 213 PM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will gradually build into the region Thursday \ninto the Labor Day weekend. This will bring a warmer, drier pattern \nto the region through Saturday night. By Sunday and Monday, the \nupper ridge may begin to flatten out across the Northern and Central \nPlains as shown by the 12Z GFS. The ECMWF maintains stronger upper \nlevel ridging. Highs Thursday through Saturday forecast to range in \nthe low to mid 90s, with some upper 90s southwest. As medium \nrange models diverge on the strength of the upper ridge Sunday \nthrough Tuesday, highs from 85 to the low 90s. Precipitation \nchances increase during this period as well, mainly during the \nevening and overnight hours. \n\nLatest ensemble guidance has increased to a 30 to 40 percent \nprobability of precipitation exceeding one tenth of an inch for the \n24 hour period ending 12Z Monday and again 12Z Tuesday.",
